{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772847664,"nonce":"wGHnvXn2KnFCb4X+8BPYcdWoB2o=","title":"Rebuild splash screen lost to race condition with daemon kill","message":"The `mandible:rebuilding` SSE event is broadcast by `POST /api/admin/rebuilding` (called from `auth-merge.sh` line 412), then `launchctl kickstart -k` immediately kills the daemon process. The browser either never receives the SSE event or loses the connection before rendering the splash.\n\n**Current flow:**\n1. `auth-merge.sh` calls `curl -sf POST /api/admin/rebuilding`\n2. Server broadcasts `mandible:rebuilding` SSE event\n3. `launchctl kickstart -k` kills and restarts the daemon immediately\n4. SSE connection drops, browser EventSource reconnects to dead server\n5. Daemon comes back, browser reloads fresh — `rebuilding` state is `false`\n6. User sees `daemon:reloaded` toast pill instead of splash\n\n**Result:** The full-page splash (Bug: 326a3e2) never visibly appears. Users see only the small toast pill after reload.\n\n**Possible fixes:**\n- Add a `sleep 1` (or similar) in `auth-merge.sh` between the curl call and `launchctl kickstart -k` to give the browser time to receive the SSE event and render the splash\n- Client-side detection: if SSE connection drops unexpectedly, show the splash (with a short debounce to avoid false positives from network blips)\n- Hybrid: broadcast the event, wait briefly, then kill. Client also detects SSE drop as a secondary trigger.\n\n**Files:**\n- `cli/auth-merge.sh` line 410-414 (broadcast + immediate kill)\n- `ui/src/app.tsx` lines 364-367 (SSE handler), 421-440 (health poll), 788-791 (splash render)","files":null}]}